  "_comment": [
    "MultiHitBoxLib hitbox profile for orespawn:the_king (BOSS-047, hitboxes align with the rigs).",
    "Generated by danger.orespawn.tools.hitbox.BossPartProfileWriter from theking.geo.json at the 1.7.10 render scale 2.1",
    "(orig ClientProxyOreSpawn.java:492, RenderTheKing scale), rest pose, body yaw 0: every part is a box fitted to the",
    "drawn cubes of the bones it covers (a flat rig: a head is CHead1-3, the jaws, eyes, teeth, nose spikes and mane,",
    "all synced through CHead1), sized [max(x extent, z extent), y extent], with the pivot taken back through MHLib's",
    "pivot rotation so the box sits ON the drawn segment, and the position the fallback offset before the first bone",
    "packet. 26 parts: body and chest, the three heads, six neck segments, four segments per wing, two legs, five tail",
    "segments. Damage modifiers as the Queen's: heads 1.0, body/necks/legs 0.5, wings/tail 0.25. main-hitbox is the",
    "1.7.10 22x24 envelope (orig TheKing.java:86), not pickable and taking no damage itself: every hit goes through a",
    "part. PlayNicely: TheKing.mhlibGetEntitySizeScale = 0.25 (render scale/4, box 5.5x6, orig :88). Replaces the",
    "hand-placed OreSpawnPartEntity layout (BOSS-002) and the KingHead sidecar box (BOSS-003), which never followed the",
    "drawn heads."
  ],
